cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "universalcefr-check: a provenance and redundancy check over the public UniversalCEFR collection"
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alvaro
    family-names: Serrano
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4701-9026"
repository-code: "https://github.com/harukicoder/universalcefr-check"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-17"
keywords:
  - CEFR
  - language proficiency
  - dataset provenance
  - data quality
  - readability
abstract: >-
  Applies a declare-then-test provenance check to the 24 public corpora of the
  UniversalCEFR collection (13 languages, 65,037 rows). The schema is uniform
  and there is no cross-corpus overlap anywhere except one pair: two entries
  declaring different repositories, papers and licences share 99.7% of their
  texts with 100% label agreement. Three corpora repeat their own texts under
  conflicting CEFR levels. Fully reproducible; redistributes no data.
